pires-forge (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security patch release: 1.0.1.
  * SHA-1 cache key replaced with SHA-256 in
    rayforge/pipeline/intent_builder.py:_hash_int. Closes the
    CodeQL 'py/weak-cryptographic-hashing-algorithm' alert on
    SHA-1 (which usedforsecurity=False does not silence in
    CodeQL even though it silences bandit/ruff B324/S324).
    The function only consumes the first 8 bytes of the digest,
    so SHA-256 (256 bits) is a drop-in replacement for SHA-1
    (160 bits) with no change in cache-key behaviour.
  * GitHub Actions workflows now declare an explicit
    `permissions: contents: read` block at the workflow level
    (with job-level write overrides where needed for
    softprops/action-gh-release, OIDC trusted publishing,
    and stale-issue labelling). Closes 18 of the
    `py/permissions-missing` CodeQL alerts. Defense-in-depth:
    a compromised step no longer has implicit repo-write
    power.
  * aiohttp bumped 3.14.1 -> 3.14.3. Closes CVE-2026-69244
    (out-of-bounds heap read in the C HTTP response parser
    error path; malformation in chunked responses can crash
    the client) and the WebSocket permessage-deflate /
    HTTP-smuggling advisories.
  * GitPython bumped 3.1.55 -> 3.1.57. Closes the
    Repo.archive() denylist bypass (--add-file /
    --add-virtual-file not in the denylist) and the
    Commit.count rev-list --output argument-injection
    primitive. CVE fixes match the advisories shipped in
    3.1.55 + the follow-up patch in 3.1.57.
  * Added an explicit `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` to
    replace GitHub's "Default" CodeQL setup, which was
    showing the "CodeQL is reporting errors" banner.
    Runs security-extended + security-and-quality query
    packs, build-mode: none (rayforge is a flat import
    tree; no compile step needed). Tagged SARIF uploads
    land under "CodeQL" in the Security tab.
  * Quoted the three step names containing colons in
    .github/workflows/verify-snap.yml (Smoke test: --help,
    --version, launch headless). The legacy GitHub Actions
    parser tolerates unquoted colons, but the strict
    GitHub workflow-validation API reports them as failed,
    which propagates as a 'failure' on every PR touching
    workflows. Closes the noise on the PRs that land
    behind this fix.
  * 4 new unit tests in tests/pipeline/test_intent_builder.py
    guard against future revert to SHA-1 (test_hash_int_uses_sha256
    is a canary spy on hashlib.sha256).
  * All 25 GitHub security alerts (3 HIGH + 22 MED) are
    now closed. `pip-audit` reports 0 vulnerabilities.

 -- Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>  Tue, 04 Aug 2026 15:30:00 +0000

pires-forge (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release of Pires Forge 1.0.0.
  * Rebrand: Rayforge -> Pires Forge (display name, AppStream ID,
    .desktop, .metainfo, Debian package, Python binary entry point).
    The Python module path 'rayforge/' and addon names
    'rayforge-addon-*' are KEPT identical to upstream for
    addon-compat and Python module compat.
  * All GitHub URLs (GITHUB_RELEASES_API, GITHUB_URL, ISSUES_URL,
    DOWNLOAD_URL) now point to yuri-schmaltz/pires-forge (this fork).
  * Application update check defaults to off (was: on, pointing to
    upstream). Users can opt-in via Settings -> Preferences.
  * Add python3-defusedxml to Depends: (required by
    rayforge.image.lightburn.importer since PR #14; blocks
    billion-laughs, XXE, and DTD-SSRF attacks).
  * i18n fix: .mo translation files are now bundled in the .deb
    (MANIFEST.in updated to include .po/.pot, plus a compile
    step in CI). Closes the silent "I selected Portuguese but
    the UI is still in English" bug.
  * Maintainer: Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>.
  * 33 regression tests in tests/shared/util/test_i18n_shipped.py
    verify every supported language ships in the binary.

 -- Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>  Sun, 03 Aug 2026 09:30:00 +0000

